Description: Fall back to SHM/MemFd buffers when DmaBuf screencast allocation fails
 On virtual GPUs (e.g. Hyper-V hyperv_drm) with software rendering (Mesa
 kms_swrast), EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import may fail with EGL_BAD_MATCH even
 though the DMA-BUF allocation itself succeeds. Without this patch, KWin
 ScreenCast stays in an infinite format-negotiation loop because
 onStreamAddBuffer returns without setting pwBuffer->user_data when
 DmaBufScreenCastBuffer::create fails.
 .
 With this patch, when DmaBuf creation fails, KWin falls through to the
 MemFd (SHM) buffer path, which works without EGL DMA-BUF import support.
Author: VMCreate <vmcreate@example.com>

--- src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp.orig	2026-08-18 13:11:39.383608155 +0000
+++ src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp	2026-08-18 13:11:39.400807173 +0000
@@ -292,9 +292,14 @@
                                                                    })) {
             pwBuffer->user_data = dmabuf;
             return;
+        } else {
+            qCWarning(KWIN_SCREENCAST) << objectName() << "DmaBuf buffer creation failed, falling back to MemFd";
         }
     }
 
+    // Fall through to MemFd: if DmaBuf creation failed (e.g. EGL DMA-BUF import
+    // not supported by the software renderer on virtual GPUs), use SHM buffers
+    // instead. This matches GNOME/mutter default MemFd ScreenCast behavior.
     if (spa_data[0].type & (1 << SPA_DATA_MemFd)) {
         if (auto memfd = MemFdScreenCastBuffer::create(pwBuffer, GraphicsBufferOptions{
                                                                      .size = QSize(m_videoFormat.size.width, m_videoFormat.size.height),
